\pard\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf5\sb100\sa200
{\f0\b\fs28\cf2 1. PIPELINE OVERVIEW\par}
\pard\ql\sb0\sa100
{\f0\fs22 The "transcript" in Voir Dire Analyst is the assembled record of all juror responses matched to their originating questions. This data flows through {\b five stages}:\par}

\pard\li720\sb60\sa60
{\f0\fs22 {\b Stage A:} Questions are generated/imported (Phase 2) and stored in the database\par}
{\f0\fs22 {\b Stage B:} Responses are recorded (Phase 4) by the owner or collaborators\par}
{\f0\fs22 {\b Stage C:} Responses are stored in the database with a questionId linking to the question\par}
{\f0\fs22 {\b Stage D:} Full case data is fetched (questions + responses + jurors) for the report\par}
{\f0\fs22 {\b Stage E:} The report/transcript is rendered and exported (EndReport, CSV, PDF, DOCX)\par}
\pard\ql\sb0\sa0
{\f0\fs2\par}

\pard\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf5\sb100\sa200
{\f0\b\fs28\cf2 2. THE CRITICAL IDENTIFIER: questionNumber vs id\par}
\pard\ql\sb0\sa100
{\f0\fs22 The system has {\b two different identifiers} for each question:\par}

\pard\li720\sb60\sa60
{\f0\fs22 {\b Database Row ID} ({\f1 questions.id}): A UUID string like "a3f8c2e1-..." \endash  internal primary key\par}
{\f0\fs22 {\b Question Number} ({\f1 questions.questionNumber}): An integer (1, 2, 3...) \endash  the user-facing sequence number\par}
\pard\ql\sb0\sa100

{\f0\fs22 {\b How they map across the system:}\par}
\pard\li720\sb60\sa60
{\f0\fs22 {\b\cf7 Frontend VoirDireQuestion.id} = questionNumber (integer) \endash  mapped in {\f1 dbQuestionToQuestion()}\par}
{\f0\fs22 {\b\cf7 Response.questionId} = questionNumber (integer) \endash  stored as integer in responses table\par}
{\f0\fs22 {\b\cf3 Collab API question objects} = return raw DB objects where {\f1 id} = UUID, {\f1 questionNumber} = integer\par}
\pard\ql\sb0\sa100

{\f0\b\fs22\cf3 \u9888  MISMATCH ZONE: The collab API returns questions with the database UUID as {\f1 id}, NOT questionNumber. The owner\'92s frontend maps {\f1 questionNumber \u8594  id}, but the collab view does not.\par}
\pard\ql\sb0\sa0
{\f0\fs2\par}

\pard\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf5\sb100\sa200
{\f0\b\fs28\cf2 3. STAGE-BY-STAGE TRACE\par}

\pard\ql\sb100\sa100
{\f0\b\fs24\cf6 STAGE A: Question Storage\par}
\pard\li360\sb60\sa60
{\f0\fs22 {\b File:} {\f1 shared/schema.ts} lines 77\endash 85\par}
{\f0\fs22 {\b Table:} {\f1 questions} \endash  columns: {\f1 id} (varchar/UUID), {\f1 caseId}, {\f1 questionNumber} (integer), {\f1 originalText}, {\f1 rephrase}, {\f1 followUps} (jsonb), {\f1 locked}\par}
{\f0\fs22 {\b Save flow:} {\f1 api.saveQuestions()} deletes all questions for the case and re-inserts them, mapping frontend {\f1 q.id} (number) to database {\f1 questionNumber}\par}
{\f0\fs22\cf4 \u2713  This stage works correctly. Questions are stored with sequential questionNumber values.\par}
\pard\ql\sb0\sa0
{\f0\fs2\par}

\pard\ql\sb100\sa100
{\f0\b\fs24\cf6 STAGE B: Response Recording\par}
\pard\li360\sb60\sa60
{\f0\fs22 {\b Owner path} ({\f1 ResponseRecording.tsx} line 329):\par}
{\f0\li720\fs20 {\f1 onRecordResponse(\{ jurorNumber: jNum, questionId: qNum, ... \})}\par}
{\f0\li720\fs20 Where {\f1 qNum = parseInt(questionNum)} and validated against {\f1 questions.find(q => q.id === qNum)}\par}
{\f0\li720\fs20 Since frontend {\f1 q.id} = questionNumber, this sends questionNumber. \cf4 \u2713  Correct\par}
\pard\li360\sb60\sa60
{\f0\fs22\cf0 {\b Collaborator (Recorder) path} ({\f1 CollaboratorView.tsx} line 348\endash 352):\par}
{\f0\li720\fs20 {\f1 const q = questions.find(q => q.questionNumber === qNum);}\par}
{\f0\li720\fs20 {\f1 payload.questionId = q ? q.questionNumber : qNum;}\par}
{\f0\li720\fs20 Collaborator gets raw DB objects from {\f1 /api/collab/questions} where questionNumber is exposed.\par}
{\f0\li720\fs20\cf4 \u2713  This sends questionNumber correctly.\par}
\pard\li360\sb60\sa60
{\f0\fs22\cf0 {\b Collaborator Quick Reaction path} ({\f1 CollaboratorView.tsx} line 309\endash 315):\par}
{\f0\li720\fs20 {\f1 const qId = activeQuestionId;}\par}
{\f0\li720\fs20 {\f1 if (qId) payload.questionId = qId;}\par}
{\f0\li720\fs20 Where {\f1 activeQuestionId} comes from the {\f1 question:set-active} WebSocket event\'92s {\f1 data.questionId} field.\par}
\pard\li360\sb100\sa60
{\f0\b\fs22\cf3 \u9888  BUG FOUND \endash  PRIOR TO FIX: The Question Asker was sending {\f1 parseInt(question.id)} where {\f1 question.id} was the database UUID string, causing {\f1 NaN} or wrong values. This was fixed to send {\f1 question.questionNumber}.\par}
\pard\li360\sb60\sa60
{\f0\b\fs22\cf3 \u9888  REMAINING CONCERN: When the questioner sends {\f1 question:set-active} with {\f1 questionId}, the recorder sets {\f1 activeQuestionId} to that value and uses it directly as {\f1 payload.questionId} in quick reactions. If the value is wrong (e.g. NaN from pre-fix tokens), all quick reactions get a bad questionId.\par}
\pard\ql\sb0\sa0
{\f0\fs2\par}

\pard\ql\sb100\sa100
{\f0\b\fs24\cf6 STAGE C: Response Storage\par}
\pard\li360\sb60\sa60
{\f0\fs22 {\b File:} {\f1 shared/schema.ts} lines 87\endash 99\par}
{\f0\fs22 {\b Table:} {\f1 responses} \endash  columns: {\f1 id} (varchar/UUID), {\f1 caseId}, {\f1 jurorNumber} (integer), {\f1 questionId} (integer, nullable), {\f1 responseText}, {\f1 side}, {\f1 questionSummary}, {\f1 followUps} (jsonb), {\f1 timestamp}, {\f1 recordedBy}\par}
{\f0\fs22 {\b Owner endpoint:} {\f1 POST /api/cases/:caseId/responses} (routes.ts line 540)\par}
{\f0\fs22 {\b Collab endpoint:} {\f1 POST /api/collab/responses} (routes.ts line 1521)\par}
{\f0\fs22 Both call {\f1 storage.createResponse()} which inserts into the responses table.\par}
{\f0\fs22\cf4 \u2713  Storage is consistent \endash  questionId is stored as-is from the request payload.\par}
{\f0\fs22\cf3 \u2717  If the request payload had a bad questionId (NaN, UUID, wrong number), it gets stored as-is.\par}
\pard\ql\sb0\sa0
{\f0\fs2\par}

\pard\ql\sb100\sa100
{\f0\b\fs24\cf6 STAGE D: Data Retrieval\par}
\pard\li360\sb60\sa60
{\f0\fs22 {\b File:} {\f1 api.ts} line 199\endash 205 ({\f1 fetchFullCase})\par}
{\f0\fs22 Fetches {\f1 /api/cases/:id/full} which returns raw DB objects for jurors, questions, responses.\par}
{\f0\fs22 {\f1 dbQuestionToQuestion()} maps {\f1 questionNumber \u8594  id} (integer)\par}
{\f0\fs22 {\f1 dbResponseToResponse()} passes {\f1 questionId} through as-is (integer)\par}
{\f0\fs22\cf4 \u2713  Retrieval logic is correct IF the stored questionId values are correct.\par}
\pard\ql\sb0\sa0
{\f0\fs2\par}

\pard\ql\sb100\sa100
{\f0\b\fs24\cf6 STAGE E: Transcript Rendering & Export\par}
\pard\li360\sb60\sa60
{\f0\fs22 {\b File:} {\f1 EndReport.tsx} line 400\endash 410 ({\f1 getQuestionText})\par}
{\f0\fs22 Core matching logic:\par}
{\f0\li720\fs20\f1 if (r.questionId) \{\par}
{\f0\li720\fs20\f1   const q = questions.find(q => q.id === r.questionId);\par}
{\f0\li720\fs20\f1   return q ? q.originalText : `Question #$\{r.questionId\}`;\par}
{\f0\li720\fs20\f1 \}\par}
\pard\li360\sb60\sa60
{\f0\fs22 This compares {\f1 q.id} (which is questionNumber after mapping) to {\f1 r.questionId} (stored integer).\par}
{\f0\fs22\cf4 \u2713  Matching logic is correct IF both values are questionNumber integers.\par}
{\f0\fs22\cf3 \u2717  If {\f1 r.questionId} was stored as NaN or a wrong value, {\f1 questions.find()} returns undefined, and the fallback text "Question #NaN" or "Question #[wrong]" appears.\par}
\pard\li360\sb60\sa60
{\f0\fs22 {\b CSV Export} ({\f1 EndReport.tsx} line 472\endash 485): Same {\f1 getQuestionText()} call per response.\par}
{\f0\fs22 {\b Strategy Export} ({\f1 exportVoirDire.ts}): Uses {\f1 doc.questions} (VoirDireDocument) and {\f1 questions} (VoirDireQuestion[]) \endash  both use questionNumber as id. \cf4 \u2713  Correct.\par}
\pard\ql\sb0\sa0
{\f0\fs2\par}

\pard\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf5\sb100\sa200
{\f0\b\fs28\cf2 4. IDENTIFIED FAILURE POINTS\par}

\pard\ql\sb100\sa60
{\f0\b\fs24\cf3 FAILURE #1: Collab questionId mismatch (FIXED but data may be corrupt)\par}
\pard\li360\sb60\sa60
{\f0\fs22 {\b Root Cause:} {\f1 QuestionAskerView.tsx} was sending {\f1 parseInt(question.id)} where {\f1 question.id} was the database UUID string (e.g. "a3f8c2e1-..."). {\f1 parseInt("a3f8c2e1-...")} returns {\f1 NaN}.\par}
{\f0\fs22 {\b Impact:} Every response recorded via quick-reaction while an asker-set question was active got {\f1 questionId: NaN} stored in the database. These responses cannot be matched to any question.\par}
{\f0\fs22 {\b Status:} Code fix applied (now sends {\f1 questionNumber}). But {\b existing response records in the database may have corrupt questionId values} (NaN or null where they should have integers).\par}
{\f0\fs22 {\b Fix needed:} Database cleanup to correct corrupted questionId values in existing responses.\par}

\pard\ql\sb100\sa60
{\f0\b\fs24\cf3 FAILURE #2: Response \u8594  Question linking completely broken for collab-recorded responses\par}
\pard\li360\sb60\sa60
{\f0\fs22 {\b Root Cause:} The {\f1 /api/collab/questions} endpoint returns raw database objects. These have {\f1 id} = UUID (string) and {\f1 questionNumber} = integer. The collaborator\'92s {\f1 handleSubmit} (CollaboratorView line 350) correctly looks up by {\f1 q.questionNumber}, so manual text submissions work.\par}
{\f0\fs22 {\b But:} The {\f1 handleQuickReaction} path (CollaboratorView line 309\endash 315) uses {\f1 activeQuestionId} directly, which came from the {\f1 question:set-active} broadcast. If the questioner sent a bad ID (pre-fix), all quick reactions inherit the bad ID.\par}
{\f0\fs22 {\b Status:} Fixed at source (questioner now sends questionNumber). Quick reactions will work correctly for new sessions.\par}

\pard\ql\sb100\sa60
{\f0\b\fs24\cf3 FAILURE #3: Server-side follow-up suggestion generation uses questionId to look up question\par}
\pard\li360\sb60\sa60
{\f0\fs22 {\b File:} {\f1 routes.ts} line 1582\par}
{\f0\fs22 {\b Code:} {\f1 const question = allQuestions.find((q) => q.questionNumber === questionId);}\par}
{\f0\fs22 This works correctly because {\f1 questionId} in the responses table is {\f1 questionNumber}.\par}
{\f0\fs22\cf4 \u2713  No issue here IF the stored questionId is correct.\par}
{\f0\fs22\cf3 \u2717  If questionId was stored as NaN, this lookup fails silently and no suggestions are generated.\par}

\pard\ql\sb100\sa60
{\f0\b\fs24\cf3 FAILURE #4: Owner ResponseRecording {\f1 question:set-active} handler\par}
\pard\li360\sb60\sa60
{\f0\fs22 {\b File:} {\f1 ResponseRecording.tsx} line 189\endash 192\par}
{\f0\fs22 {\b Code:}\par}
{\f0\li720\fs20\f1 onQuestionSetActive: useCallback((data: any) => \{\par}
{\f0\li720\fs20\f1   if (data.questionId) \{\par}
{\f0\li720\fs20\f1     setQuestionNum(data.questionId.toString());\par}
{\f0\li720\fs20\f1   \}\par}
\pard\li360\sb60\sa60
{\f0\fs22 This sets the owner\'92s question number input to the broadcast questionId. If questionId was NaN (pre-fix), {\f1 "NaN".toString()} = "NaN", which the owner sees as "NaN" in their question selector.\par}
{\f0\fs22\cf4 Post-fix: This now receives a valid questionNumber integer. \u2713  Correct.\par}
\pard\ql\sb0\sa0
{\f0\fs2\par}

\pard\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf5\sb100\sa200
