\pard\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf5\sb100\sa200
{\f0\b\fs28\cf2 8. SUMMARY & RECOMMENDED ACTIONS\par}
\pard\ql\sb0\sa100
{\f0\fs22\par
{\b Root Cause:} The Question Asker view was sending database UUIDs (parsed to NaN) instead of questionNumber integers when setting the active question. This caused every collaborator quick-reaction response to be stored with {\f1 questionId: NaN/null}, breaking the link between responses and questions. When the transcript/report renders, it cannot match these responses to any question, so they either show "Question #NaN" or are completely orphaned.\par
\par
{\b Code Fixes Applied:}\par}
\pard\li720\sb40\sa40
{\f0\fs22 1. QuestionAskerView now sends {\f1 question.questionNumber} instead of {\f1 parseInt(question.id)}\par}
{\f0\fs22 2. Follow-up tap handlers also use {\f1 questionNumber}\par}
{\f0\fs22 3. AI suggestion lookup key uses {\f1 questionNumber.toString()}\par}
{\f0\fs22 4. Role guards added on WS and HTTP endpoints\par}
{\f0\fs22 5. Duplicate broadcast removed (HTTP-only)\par}
\pard\ql\sb60\sa100
{\f0\fs22\par
{\b Remaining Actions:}\par}
\pard\li720\sb40\sa40
{\f0\fs22\cf3 1. {\b Run database diagnostic queries} (Section 6) to find corrupted response records\par}
{\f0\fs22\cf3 2. {\b Repair corrupted data} \endash  match orphaned responses to questions using questionSummary text, timestamp proximity, or recordedBy context\par}
{\f0\fs22\cf3 3. {\b Test end-to-end} with a fresh session: asker sets question \u8594  recorder quick-reacts \u8594  owner views report \u8594  export CSV/PDF\par}
\pard\ql\sb0\sa0
{\f0\fs2\par}

